  two enemies um these guys were initially  lying down pretending to be dead there  were so many ambushes in this level so  many enemies pretending to be dead that  would come at you later in the level  anyway you'll notice I took them out  with my short sword but I actually  attacked each one individually instead  of trying to cleave them both with one  swing and that's because there's a new  change to cleaving I think the ability  to damage more than one enemy with one  swing with my huge sword you'll notice I  did a cleave that damaged both enemies  but this doesn't actually seem to be  possible with the short sword I'm pretty  sure you can only hit one enemy at a  time with  small weapon swing which is an  interesting change we know that strength  weapons were underpowered in Dark Souls  and this seems to be just one of the  many ways in which strength weapons seem  to be getting above and speaking of  things that get above this bow was  really great but have a listen to what  happens here  it's pretty good what is  so these guys will surprise you they  have these running attacks where they  run at you and keep running only  stopping when they're able to swipe at  you and that's what happened there there  are really hard to deal with in melee  killing them as a mage was easy so I  assumed the bow would be a good choice  and it works pretty damn well combat  with the bow has definitely changed  as you can see loosing an arrow consumes  stamina now arrows travel faster than 1  mile per hour and arrows are able to be  loosed in quick succession while moving  also first-person aiming felt a lot more  accurate it wasn't as jumping as it is  in Dark Souls and all of this simply  points to bow builds being a really  viable way to complete the game so now  as I venture back into the dark take  note of how amazing that lighting looks  and this is on ps3 to remember just look  at those shadows mount awesome a few  notes about the environment here this  guy throws fire bombs which can blow up  and parts of the environment  you see there's black barrels to the  left there there's a little shortcut  there that a friend found it saves you a  lot of risks and takes you straight to a  bonfire I didn't take it this time  though I wanted to play through this bit  this next section can be can be really  quite tricky so I've been thinking about  it for a while and this demo really was  quite perfect  I mean level design was pretty clever  it's the small things that matter  little things like placing a door here  means that you won't be able to run past  enemies is easy enemies have sprinting  animations now and they can kill you  while you're opening a door in fact they  can kill you while you're doing pretty  much every animation there's a lot of  narrow areas areas where you had to  actually kill things in your way to  progress if you didn't kill them then  they'd come at you later while your  bottlenecked in another area and in Dark  Souls it was really easy to run past  enemies if you'd played for a long time  I have a feeling it's going to be harder  this time around another thing is the  choice of enemies  so these soldier enemies they were quite  easy so that anyone of the convention  could play but there were so many  ambushes true to the style of a Souls  game also it's worth noting that the  demo was loaded with life gems which can  be consumed over time to regain health  almost every enemy dropped one so it was  pretty obvious that they were placed  there just to make the demo easier I  doubt there'll be that abundant in the  fine  version in fact it's actually hard to  say how much of this will even be in the  final version always keep in mind when  you're judging dark souls2 footage  remember that we're like five months out  from the actual release a lot can change  alright so right now we're taking out  these two guys with this amazing sword I  have to say I love this sword  I love how strength weapons are shaping  up in general